Greeting.razor:

```razor
<h3>Hello, @Name!</h3>

@code {
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
}
```

A page uses it like this:

```razor
<Greeting Name="Ana" />
```

**What happens when the page renders?**

Toggle.razor:

```razor
<button @onclick="() => IsOn = !IsOn">@Label: @(IsOn ? "On" : "Off")</button>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public bool IsOn { get; set; }
}
```

The page (interactive):

```razor
<Toggle Label="@($"Light {clicks}")" IsOn="false" />
<button @onclick="() => clicks++">+1</button>

@code {
    private int clicks;
}
```

You click the toggle once. It shows **Light 0: On**. Then you click **+1**.

**What does the toggle show now?**

